56
00:03:46,688 --> 00:03:47,768
Flags are like

57
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:54,803
when you have an argument and it has this single dash or double dash,

58
00:03:55,523 --> 00:03:59,385
that tells to the program that this is an option.

59
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:02,686
That it should change its default behavior.

60
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:04,887
And when you go into the manual page,

61
00:04:05,067 --> 00:04:07,668
you will often see many of these flags documented.

62
00:04:08,229 --> 00:04:08,729
To be fair,

