00:04:09,389 --> 00:04:15,552
the shell doesn't require that you actually use this dash or double dash syntax.

64
00:04:16,292 --> 00:04:18,113
Everyone kind of agreed upon this,

65
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:20,054
but you will find programs that don't do it.

66
00:04:21,114 --> 00:04:29,357
So, further, the convention is that when you have a single dash it's usually like a single letter that follows.

67
00:04:29,758 --> 00:04:30,258
For example,

68
00:04:30,738 --> 00:04:37,241
-a means to also list the hidden files which are by convention as well the

